1161
01:11:23,150 --> 01:11:30,180
I naturally gravitate towards planning my tasks meticulously, utilizing calendars effectively, and ensuring no detail is overlooked.

1162
01:11:30,840 --> 01:11:36,050
Even in high-pressure situations, I tend to remain calm because I have a clear, structured plan guiding my efforts.

1163
01:11:36,430 --> 01:11:39,370
That's an invaluable skill, particularly in our line of work.

1164
01:11:40,020 --> 01:11:41,020
Anything else comes to mind?

1165
01:11:41,110 --> 01:11:41,430
Yes.

1166
01:11:41,800 --> 01:11:43,840
I also consider myself a strong communicator.

1167
01:11:44,440 --> 01:11:50,710
I genuinely enjoy collaborating with people, actively listening to their perspectives and articulating my ideas clearly.

1168
01:11:51,450 --> 01:12:01,420
In my previous role, my manager frequently commended my ability to provide feedback both kindly and clearly, which I believe significantly enhances team cohesion and effectiveness.

1169
01:12:02,120 --> 01:12:02,760
Absolutely.

1170
01:12:02,800 --> 01:12:06,650
And now for the more challenging part, what would you identify as one of your weaknesses?

1171
01:12:07,000 --> 01:12:07,380
Yes.

1172
01:12:08,120 --> 01:12:12,190
I would say that occasionally I can become overly focused on minute details.

1173
01:12:12,670 --> 01:12:20,420
I have a strong desire for everything to be perfect, which sometimes leads me to spend excess of time rechecking and refining elements that are already sufficient.

1174
01:12:20,440 --> 01:12:21,840
Perfectionism, that's a common one.

1175
01:12:21,900 --> 01:12:23,240
Has that ever presented challenges?

1176
01:12:23,420 --> 01:12:24,240
At times, yes.

1177
01:12:24,820 --> 01:12:32,110
For instance, when confronted with very tight deadlines, I've had to consciously remind myself of the adage that done is better than perfect.

1178
01:12:32,700 --> 01:12:41,580
I'm actively learning to trust my initial work more and to proactively seek feedback earlier in the process rather than continually trying to self-correct and over-fix.

1179
01:12:41,600 --> 01:12:44,370
That's a very honest answer, and it clearly shows you're working on it.

1180
01:12:45,250 --> 01:12:47,420
Any other weakness you've observed in yourself?

1181
01:12:48,330 --> 01:12:50,530
perhaps public speaking in large meetings.

1182
01:12:51,250 --> 01:12:53,070
I tend to experience a degree of nervousness.

1183
01:12:53,650 --> 01:12:59,480
I'm perfectly comfortable in smaller group settings, but when faced with a larger audience, I can feel a sense of shyness.

1184
01:13:00,300 --> 01:13:02,970
However, I am actively practicing to overcome this.

1185
01:13:03,490 --> 01:13:08,880
I joined a local public speaking group last year, and that structured practice has been incredibly beneficial.

1186
01:13:09,020 --> 01:13:09,820
That's commendable.

1187
01:13:10,220 --> 01:13:14,860
Recognizing those areas and taking proactive action truly demonstrates a growth mindset.

1188
01:13:15,490 --> 01:13:18,030
And tell me, where do you see yourself in five years?

1189
01:13:18,080 --> 01:13:19,160
That's a thoughtful question.

1190
01:13:19,620 --> 01:13:25,760
In five years, I hope to be in a role where I feel genuinely confident and extensively experienced in content strategy.

1191
01:13:26,400 --> 01:13:30,300
While I'm still in a learning phase, I find this field incredibly engaging.

1192
01:13:30,430 --> 01:13:37,200
I aspire to grow steadily, step by step, and become a highly reliable team member known for innovative ideas and emerging leadership.

1193
01:13:37,220 --> 01:13:39,240
So you're considering a leadership role eventually?

1194
01:13:39,280 --> 01:13:39,840
Yes.

1195
01:13:40,740 --> 01:13:46,890
Perhaps not an immediate large leadership position, but something along the lines of a team lead or content coordinator.

1196
01:13:47,830 --> 01:13:52,300
My desire is to not only execute tasks, but also to guide and support others.

1197
01:13:53,060 --> 01:13:58,240
I find satisfaction in helping friends or current colleagues with their writing or project planning even now.

1198
01:13:58,430 --> 01:13:59,450
That's a strong vision.

1199
01:13:59,530 --> 01:14:04,770
And are you thinking of staying in the same kind of company or do you envision moving to a different type of business?

1200
01:14:05,120 --> 01:14:10,340
I am strongly drawn to creative companies like this one, where there's ample room for new ideas and innovation.

1201
01:14:11,240 --> 01:14:17,290
While I'm not fixed on an exact type of company, I know I want to work somewhere that genuinely values creativity and its people.

1202
01:14:17,890 --> 01:14:23,740
Ultimately, I want to feel a deep sense of pride in the content I create and the tangible impact it makes.

1203
01:14:23,810 --> 01:14:28,310
Do you have any plans for further education or professional training in the next few years?

1204
01:14:28,770 --> 01:14:29,710
Yes, absolutely.

1205
01:14:30,170 --> 01:14:35,420
I'm currently exploring taking courses in UX writing or perhaps digital storytelling.

1206
01:14:36,320 --> 01:14:44,230
My goal is to gain a deeper understanding of how users interact with content online, the entire user experience, beyond just the written word.

1207
01:14:44,950 --> 01:14:51,300
If I were to join your team, I would certainly be eager to leverage any internal training programs or professional development opportunities you offer.

1208
01:14:51,400 --> 01:14:52,580
That's very good to hear.

1209
01:14:52,640 --> 01:14:55,300
We do have robust internal development programs.

1210
01:14:55,360 --> 01:14:57,410
It sounds like you've given this serious consideration.

1211
01:14:57,610 --> 01:14:57,850
Yes.

1212
01:14:58,350 --> 01:14:59,530
I strive to be realistic.

1213
01:14:59,690 --> 01:15:07,300
I understand that five years is a significant period and circumstances can change, but I find it beneficial to have a clear direction.

1214
01:15:08,060 --> 01:15:13,290
My aspiration is not just to have a job, but to build a fulfilling career that excites me every single day.

1215
01:15:13,630 --> 01:15:14,530
Well said, Emily.

1216
01:15:14,550 --> 01:15:15,410
Thank you for sharing that.

1217
01:15:15,970 --> 01:15:18,960
So, Emily, why should we hire you over other candidates?

1218
01:15:19,120 --> 01:15:27,350
I believe you should hire me because I offer a unique combination of creativity, responsibility, and an unwavering motivation to contribute meaningfully.

1219
01:15:28,150 --> 01:15:29,390
I'm not just seeking a job.

1220
01:15:29,810 --> 01:15:32,020
I genuinely want to be an integral part of your team.

1221
01:15:32,640 --> 01:15:37,980
I pay meticulous attention to detail, yet I also maintain a clear understanding of the broader strategic picture.

1222
01:15:38,840 --> 01:15:48,030
When I approach any project, my fundamental question is always, how does this piece of content or strategy best serve both the company's objectives and its target audience?

1223
01:15:48,420 --> 01:15:49,550
That's a solid mindset.

1224
01:15:49,770 --> 01:15:51,610
Can you provide a concrete example?

1225
01:15:51,880 --> 01:15:52,380
Certainly.

1226
01:15:53,060 --> 01:15:56,420
At my previous role, I developed a weekly post series for our Instagram account.

1227
01:15:57,020 --> 01:16:00,130
My effort went beyond merely creating aesthetically pleasing images.

1228
01:16:00,910 --> 01:16:05,180
I consistently monitored comments and messages to gauge audience preferences and emerging needs.

1229
01:16:05,680 --> 01:16:14,710
Within a month, we observed a significant increase in engagement, and we even had new customers specifically mentioned discovering us through those posts, demonstrating a clear return on investment.

1230
01:16:14,790 --> 01:16:15,730
That's real impact.

1231
01:16:16,250 --> 01:16:20,200
And beyond skills, what do you think you bring as a person to our team?

1232
01:16:20,280 --> 01:16:23,280
I consider myself a highly positive and proactive individual.

1233
01:16:24,040 --> 01:16:30,070
I genuinely enjoy collaborating with others, actively solving problems and maintaining forward momentum.

1234
01:16:30,830 --> 01:16:35,730
I strive to remain calm and composed under pressure, and I possess a strong sense of perseverance.

1235
01:16:36,930 --> 01:16:42,400
If an approach isn't working, I'm quick to ask clarifying questions, iterate or seek assistance.

1236
01:16:42,420 --> 01:16:47,480
I fundamentally believe that effective teamwork is built on mutual listening and the generous sharing of ideas.

1237
01:16:47,580 --> 01:16:49,100
That's incredibly important here.

1238
01:16:49,180 --> 01:16:50,830
We deeply value collaboration.

1239
01:16:51,150 --> 01:16:56,340
Yes, and I sincerely believe I would integrate seamlessly and contribute positively to your team.

1240
01:16:57,160 --> 01:17:03,770
While I may not possess every single answer yet, I'm exceptionally eager to learn, grow, and commit my absolute best effort from day one.

1241
01:17:04,300 --> 01:17:04,960
Thank you, Emily.

1242
01:17:04,980 --> 01:17:05,860
That's a strong answer.

1243
01:17:06,280 --> 01:17:08,970
Now tell me about a time you faced a significant challenge at work.

1244
01:17:09,110 --> 01:17:11,300
Yes, I recall one situation very distinctly.

1245
01:17:12,160 --> 01:17:20,050
At my last job, we were in the midst of a campaign for a local brand, and everything was progressing smoothly until the client unexpectedly changed the deadline.

1246
01:17:20,870 --> 01:17:25,050
They suddenly required everything to be completed one full week earlier than initially planned.

1247
01:17:25,410 --> 01:17:27,150
That sounds incredibly stressful.

1248
01:17:27,300 --> 01:17:28,040
It certainly was.

1249
01:17:28,380 --> 01:17:35,970
We had a substantial amount of work to complete rapidly – the designs, all the social media posts, and the final client presentation.

1250
01:17:36,200 --> 01:17:42,760
Initially, I felt quite overwhelmed, and frankly, the entire team was a bit disoriented on how to proceed.

1251
01:17:43,140 --> 01:17:45,020
So what specific actions did you take?

1252
01:17:45,690 --> 01:17:50,160
I proactively approached my manager and offered to help organize the revised schedule.

1253
01:17:50,440 --> 01:17:58,730
I immediately created a detailed list, identifying remaining tasks, categorizing them by urgency, and clearly dividing the workload among my teammates.

1254
01:17:59,530 --> 01:18:07,380
I also extended my assistance to a colleague who was falling behind on copywriting for one of the posts, ensuring we kept moving forward as a cohesive unit.

1255
01:18:07,660 --> 01:18:09,530
That demonstrates excellent initiative.

1256
01:18:09,730 --> 01:18:10,090
Thank you.

1257
01:18:10,690 --> 01:18:14,510
In the end, despite the sudden shift, we managed to deliver the project on time.

1258
01:18:15,350 --> 01:18:19,620
It wasn't entirely perfect, but the client was exceedingly happy with the outcome.

1259
01:18:19,870 --> 01:18:25,540
The team also expressed their gratitude for my efforts in helping maintain calm and clarity during a stressful period.

1260
01:18:25,760 --> 01:18:28,260
It sounds like you maintain a remarkable focus under pressure.

1261
01:18:28,320 --> 01:18:32,170
Yes, I learned invaluable lessons from that experience.

1262
01:18:32,190 --> 01:18:37,100
Challenges are far easier to navigate when you remain organized and maintain open lines of communication.

1263
01:18:37,760 --> 01:18:40,040
That situation truly helped me grow professionally.

1264
01:18:40,140 --> 01:18:40,840
Great example.

1265
01:18:40,880 --> 01:18:41,500
Thank you, Emily.

1266
01:18:42,240 --> 01:18:46,450
Okay, Emily, how do you typically handle pressure or stressful situations?

1267
01:18:46,870 --> 01:18:53,280
I believe stress is an inherent part of nearly every job, but our response to it makes all the difference.

1268
01:18:54,140 --> 01:18:59,050
For me, when I feel pressure building, my immediate response is to pause and take a few deep breaths.

1269
01:18:59,890 --> 01:19:05,040
I consciously try to remain calm and think clearly, even when circumstances feel urgent or chaotic.

1270
01:19:05,580 --> 01:19:06,880
That's a very smart first step.

1271
01:19:07,080 --> 01:19:09,280
And what do you usually do after that initial calm?

1272
01:19:09,350 --> 01:19:14,410
I systematically break down large, overwhelming tasks into smaller, more manageable steps.

1273
01:19:15,010 --> 01:19:19,820
If I'm facing a major deadline, I ask myself, what is the very next actionable step I can take right now?

1274
01:19:20,720 --> 01:19:22,820
This approach helps me regain a sense of control.

1275
01:19:23,380 --> 01:19:29,650
I also quickly create a simple plan or a checklist so I can visually track my progress, which provides a positive psychological boost.

1276
01:19:29,910 --> 01:19:33,950
And how does that strategy translate when you're working within a team, not just alone?

1277
01:19:33,970 --> 01:19:38,150
In team environments, I prioritize maintaining open and honest communication.

1278
01:19:39,130 --> 01:19:45,400
If I'm feeling stressed, I express it, not in a negative or complaining way, but to be transparent and proactive.

1279
01:19:46,060 --> 01:19:49,010
I might say something like, this deadline is particularly tight.

1280
01:19:49,320 --> 01:19:52,770
Can we briefly review our priorities together to ensure alignment?

1281
01:19:53,510 --> 01:19:58,600
I believe asking for clarity or support is always preferable to silently struggling and becoming overwhelmed.

1282
01:19:58,880 --> 01:20:02,760
Have you ever experienced a moment when the stress became truly overwhelming?

1283
01:20:02,880 --> 01:20:03,560
Yes, I have.

1284
01:20:03,660 --> 01:20:12,270
Actually, last year we had a week where two major projects unexpectedly overlapped, and a key teammate became ill, leaving me with additional responsibilities.

1285
01:20:12,950 --> 01:20:19,180
I began to feel genuinely exhausted, and inadvertently I made a minor error in a social media post that went live, which made me feel terrible.

1286
01:20:19,360 --> 01:20:21,120
How did you recover from that experience?

1287
01:20:21,170 --> 01:20:24,610
I immediately informed my manager, and we swiftly corrected the post.

1288
01:20:25,750 --> 01:20:35,410
But more importantly, that incident made me realize the crucial need to integrate short breaks into my day, stay hydrated, and ensure I was eating properly even when incredibly busy.

1289
01:20:36,150 --> 01:20:39,270
I also began utilizing a time tracking app to enhance my focus.

1290
01:20:39,990 --> 01:20:44,540
That demanding week underscored that managing stress isn't solely about work strategies.

1291
01:20:45,080 --> 01:20:47,240
It's also profoundly about self-care.

1292
01:20:47,480 --> 01:20:49,040
That's a truly valuable lesson.

1293
01:20:49,060 --> 01:20:51,620
It sounds like you've learned a great deal from your experiences.

1294
01:20:51,760 --> 01:20:51,980
Yes.

1295
01:20:52,280 --> 01:21:00,030
Now, my approach is to prioritize staying calm, maintaining organization, and proactively seeking support when necessary.

1296
01:21:00,870 --> 01:21:03,240
I no longer perceive pressure as inherently negative.

1297
01:21:03,720 --> 01:21:07,740
Handled constructively, it can actually be a powerful catalyst for personal and professional growth.

1298
01:21:08,040 --> 01:21:08,660
Thank you, Emily.

1299
01:21:08,680 --> 01:21:10,670
I truly appreciate your thoughtful and honest answer.

1300
01:21:10,910 --> 01:21:12,470
Now, let's discuss salary for a moment.

1301
01:21:12,830 --> 01:21:14,630
What are your salary expectations, Emily?

1302
01:21:14,800 --> 01:21:15,540
Thank you for asking.

1303
01:21:15,940 --> 01:21:26,630
I've conducted thorough research on similar roles within the city, and my understanding is that the average salary for this position typically falls within the range of $45,000 to $50,000 annually.

1304
01:21:27,290 --> 01:21:33,300
Based on my existing experience and developed skills, I believe compensation within that range would be fair and appropriate.

1305
01:21:33,420 --> 01:21:34,420
That's a reasonable range.

1306
01:21:34,580 --> 01:21:36,870
Is salary your absolute top priority?

1307
01:21:37,450 --> 01:21:39,590
Not necessarily my sole priority.

1308
01:21:40,070 --> 01:21:52,140
While I certainly expect to be compensated fairly for my contributions, I genuinely value growth opportunities, a supportive learning environment, and being an integral part of a positive team culture just as much.

1309
01:21:52,910 --> 01:21:58,220
If there are clear pathways to develop my skills and advance within the company, that carries significant weight for me.

1310
01:21:58,520 --> 01:21:59,020
I understand.

1311
01:21:59,040 --> 01:22:00,760
And are you flexible regarding that range?

1312
01:22:00,780 --> 01:22:01,200
Yes, I am.

1313
01:22:01,800 --> 01:22:10,850
I'm certainly open to discussing it further, depending on the comprehensive offer, including the full benefits package, available training programs, and the specific responsibilities of the role itself.

1314
01:22:11,600 --> 01:22:16,900
My primary objective is to find a truly good fit where I can engage in meaningful work and continuously grow.

1315
01:22:17,220 --> 01:22:19,160
That's a very pragmatic approach.

1316
01:22:19,180 --> 01:22:21,530
Thank you for being so honest and well-prepared.

1317
01:22:21,630 --> 01:22:21,990
Thank you.

1318
01:22:22,730 --> 01:22:26,450
My aim is always for a win-win scenario for both parties.

1319
01:22:26,700 --> 01:22:30,230
And Emily, do you prefer working independently or as part of a team?

1320
01:22:30,990 --> 01:22:32,090
That's an excellent question.

1321
01:22:32,890 --> 01:22:34,230
Honestly, I enjoy both.

1322
01:22:34,870 --> 01:22:39,130
And I believe each mode has its distinct advantages depending on the task.

1323
01:22:39,150 --> 01:22:49,850
When I'm engaged in tasks that demand deep focus, such as creative writing or meticulous editing, I find working independently allows me to concentrate more effectively and manage my time with greater autonomy.

1324
01:22:50,310 --> 01:22:56,570
However, when it comes to tackling larger projects or complex problem solving, I genuinely thrive in a team environment.

1325
01:22:56,820 --> 01:22:59,290
So you'd say you're comfortable and adept at both styles.

1326
01:22:59,530 --> 01:23:00,270
Yes, absolutely.

1327
01:23:00,590 --> 01:23:05,070
For instance, in my previous role, I was frequently responsible for crafting our weekly blog posts.

1328
01:23:05,100 --> 01:23:07,100
That aspect was largely independent.

1329
01:23:07,120 --> 01:23:10,940
I conducted research, drafted content, and performed initial edits on my own.

1330
01:23:11,340 --> 01:23:18,530
Yet before publishing, I consistently met with the graphic designer and the marketing manager to discuss the layout, optimal timing, and overall messaging.

1331
01:23:19,110 --> 01:23:21,920
That collaborative phase was essential and highly productive.

1332
01:23:22,340 --> 01:23:27,020
And how do you typically approach group decisions or brainstorming sessions?

1333
01:23:27,130 --> 01:23:28,170
I truly value them.

1334
01:23:28,630 --> 01:23:34,900
I firmly believe that the most robust and innovative ideas often emerge from actively listening to diverse perspectives.

1335
01:23:35,480 --> 01:23:41,850
Sometimes, a seemingly simple comment from someone else can unexpectedly provide me with an entirely new viewpoint.

1336
01:23:42,390 --> 01:23:45,390
Furthermore, I'm not hesitant to voice my ideas in meetings.

1337
01:23:45,910 --> 01:23:49,550
I strive to offer constructive suggestions while also listening intently to others.

1338
01:23:50,180 --> 01:23:52,800
It's fundamentally important to respect all voices within a group.

1339
01:23:53,100 --> 01:23:55,820
What happens when there's a disagreement within a group setting?

1340
01:23:56,020 --> 01:23:58,940
Disagreements are, of course, a natural part of collaborative work.

1341
01:23:59,890 --> 01:24:03,810
I believe the key lies in maintaining open communication and mutual respect.

1342
01:24:04,890 --> 01:24:09,020
If someone expresses disagreement with my idea, I don't take it personally.

1343
01:24:09,620 --> 01:24:12,380
Instead, I calmly ask, could you explain your reasoning?

1344
01:24:13,930 --> 01:24:17,370
This approach allows me to learn and understand their perspective.

1345
01:24:17,590 --> 01:24:27,100
Conversely, if I disagree with someone, I endeavor to articulate my viewpoint in a kind and clear manner, perhaps by saying, I see your point, but what if we consider this alternative approach?

1346
01:24:27,740 --> 01:24:32,790
My focus is always on collaboratively seeking a solution rather than merely winning an argument.

1347
01:24:33,030 --> 01:24:33,690
Very well said.

1348
01:24:34,440 --> 01:24:38,680
And when you work alone, how do you ensure you stay motivated and productive?

1349
01:24:39,200 --> 01:24:47,500
When working independently, I typically set small, achievable goals for myself, such as completing a specific section before lunch or reviewing everything by a certain time.

1350
01:24:48,240 --> 01:24:51,560
I also make it a point to take short, refreshing drugs to maintain mental clarity.

1351
01:24:52,250 --> 01:24:57,680
I'm quite self-disciplined, and I find a strong sense of satisfaction from checking off items on my task list.

1352
01:24:57,700 --> 01:24:59,660
It provides a tangible feeling of progress.

1353
01:24:59,980 --> 01:25:01,600
Sounds like you have very strong work habits.

1354
01:25:02,560 --> 01:25:03,510
One last question on this.

1355
01:25:04,170 --> 01:25:09,350
If you had to choose only one, working alone or in a team, which would you ultimately prefer?

1356
01:25:11,000 --> 01:25:15,020
If I had to make an exclusive choice, I would lean towards working in a team.

1357
01:25:15,820 --> 01:25:22,710
I genuinely enjoy the dynamic of being around people, sharing ideas, and the collective experience of building something significant together.

1358
01:25:23,590 --> 01:25:31,100
However, I do recognize my need for periods of quiet, uninterrupted time during the day for deep thought and creative output.

1359
01:25:31,840 --> 01:25:38,830
So while a blend is truly ideal, if pressed, the collaborative energy of a team is where I ultimately feel most energized.

1360
01:25:38,890 --> 01:25:39,590
Thank you, Emily.

1361
01:25:39,610 --> 01:25:41,370
I appreciate your honest and thoughtful answer.

1362
01:25:41,430 --> 01:25:42,260
All right, Emily.

1363
01:25:42,350 --> 01:25:45,240
Now tell me about a time you experienced a significant failure.

1364
01:25:45,740 --> 01:25:46,560
What did you learn from it?

1365
01:25:47,000 --> 01:25:47,240
Yes.

1366
01:25:47,680 --> 01:25:50,770
There's one particular experience that profoundly taught me a valuable lesson.

1367
01:25:51,590 --> 01:25:56,350
It occurred during my internship when I was assisting with the planning of a small online event for our new customers.

1368
01:25:57,040 --> 01:26:03,020
My specific responsibility was to ensure the invitation emails were sent out with all the correct links at precise event times.

1369
01:26:03,240 --> 01:26:04,310
And what transpired?

1370
01:26:04,370 --> 01:26:07,660
Well, I sent out the email, but I made a critical error.

1371
01:26:08,200 --> 01:26:10,820
I inadvertently copied the incorrect time for the event.

1372
01:26:11,260 --> 01:26:13,520
I simply didn't double-check that specific detail.

1373
01:26:14,430 --> 01:26:18,430
As a result, some attendees showed up late, and a few even missed the event entirely.

1374
01:26:19,250 --> 01:26:24,660
The team was understandably surprised, and my manager had to promptly send an apology message to all the guests.

1375
01:26:24,960 --> 01:26:26,380
That must have been a difficult moment.

1376
01:26:26,510 --> 01:26:28,700
Yes, I felt absolutely terrible.

1377
01:26:29,200 --> 01:26:31,100
I believed I had completely undermined the event.

1378
01:26:31,510 --> 01:26:32,790
I was incredibly embarrassed.

1379
01:26:33,330 --> 01:26:36,180
However, my manager handled it with remarkable kindness.

1380
01:26:36,820 --> 01:26:39,930
She sat down with me and said, Everyone makes mistakes, Emily.

1381
01:26:40,290 --> 01:26:42,820
What truly matters is what you choose to do next.

1382
01:26:42,850 --> 01:26:45,030
That's an excellent way to approach such a situation.

1383
01:26:45,210 --> 01:26:45,670
Exactly.

1384
01:26:46,210 --> 01:26:49,420
So I immediately drafted a sincere apology to the entire team.

1385
01:26:50,140 --> 01:27:00,230
And to prevent future occurrences, I developed a comprehensive checklist system for myself to meticulously review all important details before sending any public communication.

1386
01:27:01,170 --> 01:27:08,340
I also proactively began asking another intern to double check my work whenever it involved external communication, ensuring a second pair of eyes.

1387
01:27:08,800 --> 01:27:11,710
That sounds like a highly responsible and proactive reaction.

1388
01:27:11,840 --> 01:27:12,160
Thank you.

1389
01:27:12,480 --> 01:27:16,310
Since that experience, I've become significantly more detail-oriented and careful.

1390
01:27:16,890 --> 01:27:22,480
I learned that even seemingly small details like a time or a link can have substantial consequences.

1391
01:27:23,280 --> 01:27:26,500
And crucially, I learned not to be paralyzed by mistakes.

1392
01:27:27,160 --> 01:27:30,490
While they can be painful, they serve as powerful catalysts for growth.

1393
01:27:30,670 --> 01:27:32,210
That's a truly powerful lesson.

1394
01:27:32,490 --> 01:27:35,030
I genuinely appreciate your honesty and self-awareness.

1395
01:27:35,070 --> 01:27:35,440
Thank you.

1396
01:27:35,850 --> 01:27:40,760
I always strive to transform any setback or failure into a constructive learning opportunity.

1397
01:27:40,920 --> 01:27:43,100
Before we conclude, Emily, do you have any questions for us?

1398
01:27:43,420 --> 01:27:44,220
Yes, thank you.

1399
01:27:44,300 --> 01:27:44,960
I have a couple.

1400
01:27:45,740 --> 01:27:48,970
